  "resolved_items": [
    {
      "item": "direct judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "The factorization mathematics is settled positively. The source-to-model correspondence remains unresolved: neither completeness of the modeled current data nor agreement of effective domains is established. This is an evidential limitation, not a demonstrated counterexample.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 10, Section 1.7, specifies determination by current-time data without defining its domain. D001 and D015 quantify over every history of real vector fields."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "The blind translation accurately reconstructs the supplied declaration. Its mathematical interpretation requires no correction; its identification with the complete source characterization remains conditional.",
      "primary_evidence": "Both dossiers expand the left side to equality of outputs for histories with equal final states and the right side to existence of a factorization through that final state."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "Retain undetermined because the unresolved correspondence prevents an unconditional faithfulness judgment. No genuine strengthening or definite weakening has been established.",
      "primary_evidence": "The target fixes S = Cell → Fin m → Real and H = Fin (n+1) → S; the selected source paragraph specifies neither a complete data object nor an admissible-history domain."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "Retain undetermined independently of agreement between judges. The translation is exact, but that does not settle whether its chosen model covers the source's intended methods.",
      "primary_evidence": "The blind translation explicitly admits all histories and a total advance; printed page 10 gives only the prose temporal-dependence characterization."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D001 unclear",
      "resolution": "Declaration meaning is fully resolved: the abbreviation asserts history independence relative to the entire final numerical field. Only its identification with all source current-time data remains uncertain.",
      "primary_evidence": "D001 is Function.FactorsThrough advance (fun history => history (Fin.last n)); D015 expands this into a universal implication comparing pairs of histories."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D003 unclear",
      "resolution": "Existential quantification introduces one step for each fixed n and advance. It adds no solvability assumption inside the supplied total-function model: define step(s) = advance(fun _ => s). Its source-domain applicability remains uncertain.",
      "primary_evidence": "Exists occurs inside the universal n and advance binders. Every s has the constant history as a preimage under the final-state projection."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D011 unclear",
      "resolution": "Real has no disputed operator semantics here. Real vector fields are compatible with the numerical-state context; the unresolved issue concerns completeness of the data representation, not the real-number type itself.",
      "primary_evidence": "D011 supplies Real as the scalar type, without arithmetic or topology in the target. Printed pages 10–11 describe spatial numerical values Q and m-vector systems."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D015 unclear",
      "resolution": "FactorsThrough means constancy on fibers, not an independently assumed representing map. Its universal domain is exactly the full history type. This meaning is resolved; correspondence of that domain to source applicability remains uncertain.",
      "primary_evidence": "D015 has body ∀ ⦃a b⦄, Eq (f a) (f b) → Eq (g a) (g b)."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C02 unclear",
      "resolution": "Spatial, component, and temporal indexing are appropriate. Arbitrary Cell permits full spatial fields, and Fin m harmlessly reindexes components. Whether this field exhausts current-time data remains unresolved.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 10 distinguishes spatial subscripts and time superscripts; printed page 11 specifies m-vectors. The Lean state is Cell → Fin m → Real."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
      "resolution": "Totality is a restriction of the supplied advance type, not a theorem conclusion. The source does not establish that every intended method has this full input domain, so the applicability question remains unresolved.",
      "primary_evidence": "advance has type (Fin (n+1) → S) → S without an admissibility predicate. Section 1.7 does not specify admissible inputs."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C05 unclear",
      "resolution": "Complete current-to-next dependence is represented within the model. No separate source conclusion about accuracy, convergence, or a particular formula is missing. Completeness of the determining data remains uncertain.",
      "primary_evidence": "The source requires determination entirely by current-time data; the target's representing function receives precisely history (Fin.last n)."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C08 unclear",
      "resolution": "No exact-versus-numerical conflation is present. History entries can represent Q at successive levels and the output the next Q. The only unresolved identity is between the whole Q field and all determining current data.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 10 places the sentence in the paragraph defining Q as a numerical approximation. The target contains no exact solution q or equality between q and Q."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C10 unclear",
      "resolution": "Arbitrary spatial types and degenerate component counts are harmless extensions of this dependence characterization. Restriction to total advances on unrestricted histories is not established as harmless and cannot be credited as stronger content.",
      "primary_evidence": "Cell and m are universally quantified, while advance is constrained by its total function type. The source supplies no matching effective-domain specification."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item N01 unclear",
      "resolution": "The abstract transition has the correct temporal information structure. A concrete numerical formula is unnecessary for this source sentence. Coverage of the source's execution domain and full inputs remains uncertain.",
      "primary_evidence": "Section 1.7 characterizes one-step dependence without an update formula. The target sends a history ending at n to an output state through a current-state projection."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
      "resolution": "No additional numerical existence or uniqueness theorem is concealed in the factorization. A supplied total advance and fiber constancy determine a unique step by constant histories. The initial choice of total domain remains unverified against the source.",
      "primary_evidence": "For p(h)=h(n), p(fun _ => s)=s. Consequently step(s)=advance(fun _ => s), and any representing step must have this value."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C02 unclear",
      "resolution": "The translated types match the declaration exactly and support the source's spatial vector notation. Completeness of S as the data object and agreement of admissible domains remain unresolved.",
      "primary_evidence": "The blind translation states S = Cell → Fin m → ℝ and H = Fin (n+1) → S; these are exactly the supplied elaborated types."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C03 unclear",
      "resolution": "Witness dependence is correct: step may vary with n and advance, but not with a particular history. No autonomous update is imposed. The uncertainty about all-history scope is an effective-domain issue rather than a Skolemization error.",
      "primary_evidence": "The elaborated target places Exists step after the universal n and advance binders and requires equality of whole functions."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
      "resolution": "The translation correctly exposes totality and absence of admissibility restrictions. These are genuine model choices whose agreement with the source remains unresolved.",
      "primary_evidence": "The target quantifies advance : H → S and D015 compares all a,b : H; printed page 10 does not define H or an admissible subset."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C05 unclear",
      "resolution": "The translated equivalence fully captures determination by the modeled current state. The source does not settle whether any independently varying current data lie outside that state.",
      "primary_evidence": "The source uses 'data at time t_n'; the target and translation give step only the final real vector field."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C07 unclear",
      "resolution": "The relation-strength concern is resolved within the model: fiber constancy and exact factorization are equivalent in both directions. This is a characterization, not an assertion that every advance is one-step. Source applicability remains a separate unresolved matter.",
      "primary_evidence": "D008 is Iff. Using constant histories proves the forward mathematical implication; substituting equal projected states into step proves the reverse."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C08 unclear",
      "resolution": "Lack of a numerical label in the blind translation is not evidence of object conflation. The source context supplies the interpretation as numerical fields. Completeness of the varying current data remains unresolved.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 10 introduces Q immediately before the selected sentence. Neither the translation nor declaration identifies these states with an exact PDE solution."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C10 unclear",
      "resolution": "The spatial and component abstractions are compatible with the stated notation. The effective-domain choice remains unresolved, and any resulting loss of applicability would not qualify as faithful strength.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed pages 10–11 permit spatial numerical arrays and m-vectors; the target additionally chooses all histories of these arrays as the advance domain."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
      "resolution": "The enumerated boundary cases are coherent and do not independently obstruct faithfulness. At n=0 there is no earlier entry; for empty Cell or m=0 the state space is a singleton. Admissibility uncertainty belongs to the domain issue.",
      "primary_evidence": "Fin.last n has value n in Fin (n+1), including n=0. Empty indexing makes Cell → Fin m → Real a singleton in the stated degenerate cases."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N01 unclear",
      "resolution": "The history-to-next-state interpretation is supported by the source context and the current-state selector. No concrete scheme is required. The unresolved linkage concerns full input data and effective domain.",
      "primary_evidence": "The selected sentence discusses successive numerical time levels; the declaration separates a history ending at n from the output of advance."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N04 unclear",
      "resolution": "Resolve this concern positively. Real-valued arrays may represent numerical approximations, and exact equality of deterministic update functions does not assert exact solution of the PDE or absence of numerical error.",
      "primary_evidence": "Section 1.7 identifies Q as a numerical approximation; the target has no exact-solution variable, error bound, or asserted equality to q."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
      "resolution": "The representing step is constructible and uniquely determined in the given model. No explicit-computation or implicit-solver requirement is introduced. Agreement of the assumed total domain with the source remains unresolved.",
      "primary_evidence": "The projection is surjective by constant histories, and D006 expands composition to ordinary function application."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left implication lean_implies_source unclear",
      "resolution": "Retain unclear for the full source comparison. For a method represented by the supplied advance and complete current state, factorization gives the source dependence condition immediately; coverage of all intended source methods is not established.",
      "primary_evidence": "advance(h)=step(h(n)) excludes earlier-history dependence, but the source does not identify its data and domain with S and H."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left implication source_implies_lean unclear",
      "resolution": "Retain unclear as a source-representation judgment. The mathematical equivalence is valid independently, but source prose does not settle the model's complete data object or universal history domain.",
      "primary_evidence": "Constant histories establish the Lean equivalence. Printed page 10 supplies no identification of all current-time data with S or admissible histories with H."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication translation_implies_source unclear",
      "resolution": "Retain unclear for the same unresolved correspondence, not because the translation lacks an assertion that a particular scheme is one-step. A characterization need not classify a particular scheme.",
      "primary_evidence": "The source sentence is a general characterization; the blind translation faithfully describes the universal biconditional in the declaration."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication source_implies_translation unclear",
      "resolution": "Retain unclear for source faithfulness. Once the data and domain correspondence is supplied, determination and factorization agree; the present source evidence does not supply that correspondence.",
      "primary_evidence": "The translation's universal history scope and total step are explicit. Section 1.7 leaves the data object and admissible domain unspecified."
    }
  ],
  "implications": {
    "lean_implies_source": {
      "verdict": "unclear",
      "reasoning": "Under the interpretation that S is the complete current-time data and advance represents the numerical transition on the intended domain, the target characterizes exactly determination from the current level. It preserves full spatial dependence and permits a different step for each n and advance. The supplied evidence does not establish that this total-history model covers the source's full intended scope. Therefore conditional agreement cannot be promoted to an unconditional source-faithfulness implication."
    },
    "source_implies_lean": {
      "verdict": "unclear",
      "reasoning": "Within the Lean model, the equivalence follows directly by defining step(s)=advance(fun _ => s), with the converse following from composition. This mathematical fact does not establish that the source's current-time data are exactly S or that its intended dependence condition is evaluated on every element of H. The direction remains unclear as a comparison of source and formal meanings, rather than as a question about independent provability of the Lean proposition."
    }
  },
  "classification": "undetermined",
  "accepted": false,
  "remaining_uncertainties": [
    "Whether the spatial real m-vector field represents all independently varying current-time data. Fixed method parameters and prescribed time dependence can be captured by the fixed advance, but the source does not enumerate the data.",
    "Whether total advances on every finite history preserve the source's effective domain. Restriction to admissible histories or partial updates is neither specified nor excluded by the selected passage."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "unresolved-data-and-domain-correspondence",
      "evidence": "Printed page 10 characterizes determination by current-time data without specifying a data object or admissibility domain. The target fixes S = Cell → Fin m → Real and uses a total advance on all H = Fin (n+1) → S.",
      "impact": "Full source equivalence remains unestablished. This is not sufficient evidence for a definite mismatch, and any actual restriction of applicability must not be labeled stronger."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "exact-factorization-and-nonvacuity",
      "evidence": "D001 and D015 express constancy on fibers of h ↦ h(n); D002, D003, D006, and D008 express exact existential factorization. Constant histories supply a section. With one cell, m=1, and n=1, returning the current state satisfies the property, while returning the initial state fails it on histories sharing a final state.",
      "impact": "The mathematical characterization is exact and substantive. It is not sustained only by impossible premises or degenerate state spaces."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "resolved-indexing-and-quantity-roles",
      "evidence": "D004, D005, D007, D009, D010, D012, D013, and D014 give ordinary indices 0 through n and final index n. D011 supplies real components without an exact-solution assertion. The source's pages 10–11 support spatial numerical fields and vector components.",
      "impact": "No off-by-one, same-cell locality, autonomous-update, explicit-method, or exact-versus-approximate substitution is present. These concerns do not justify withholding acceptance independently of the remaining correspondence questions."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "I inspected the attached primary-source pages and the complete inline declarations, dependency inventory, reuse records, translation, and judgments. The source supports the intended temporal dependence interpretation, and the declaration supplies a correct nonvacuous factorization characterization. Rechecking the dependencies resolves their mathematical meanings; reuse hashes alone were not treated as evidence of source applicability. Several checklist uncertainties concern harmless indexing, witness dependence, boundary cases, or numerical-state labeling and are resolved positively. The remaining substantive uncertainty is the correspondence between the source's unspecified data and domain and the target's precise total-function model. Neither acceptance nor a definite directional mismatch is justified by the supplied evidence, so the classification remains undetermined. No independent source-byte or rendering-hash recomputation is claimed."
}
